<title>UK: Trafigura says it signed Iraqi oil purchase deal.</title>
<headline>Trafigura says it signed Iraqi oil purchase deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private Dutch oil trading firm Trafigura has signed a three-month deal with Iraq to buy crude oil, a company spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>He said the contract was approved by the United Nations on Friday and he expected to load his first cargo at the end of December.</p>
<p>He would not confirm the exact volume of oil involved, but said it was between 10,000 and 30,000 barrels per day.</p>
<p>-- Tom Ashby, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
</text>
